WEBVTT

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.790
Mary!

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.290
Lucy!

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.080
Help me out!

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.120
Somebody got sick!

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.370
This way!

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.040
Moriarty?

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:50.200
"Men's Bathroom"

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.580
"Men's Bathroom"

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.580
Yup. Yup. Yeah.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.290
"Men's Bathroom"

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.290
Take care of it.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:55.700
"Men's Bathroom"

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.120
"Men's Bathroom"

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.120
James- <i>sama</i> !

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.330
That's...

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:14.200
When a single flower blooms on the bloodstained stage,
your hopes will be shattered into dust.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.700
That's what the bomber said
in his message, right?

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.330
The bombs in the lunches
were a game set by Moriarty.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:25.370
That car was Albert's real target.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.700
But what was Moran's hope?

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:33.870
The car that was bombed
belonged to Richard D. Godain.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.540
Moran was only able to remain a Ward Mayor

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:41.370
because of his backing and incredible influence.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.200
So what?

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.660
Now that Godain's kicked the bucket,
Moran can't be mayor anymore?

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.620
Yup. That's right.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:59.250
I don't know how much
of what Moriarty said is true,

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.830
but we need to hear it from him personally.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.870
Lestrade's here.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:08.540
He may know where Moriarty is.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:12.080
Sherlock! John!

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.000
If you find something, let me know.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.950
I need to talk to Hudson.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.080
It's okay, right?

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.750
Of course.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:07.410
And thus the Grand Guignol reached
its end at the hands of Albert Trevor!

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:08.450
Damn it! Damn it all!

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:12.290
"Moriarty Savors"

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:12.290
Damn it! Damn it all!

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.790
"Moriarty Savors"

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.790
Fine. Contact me when you know more.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.870
Godain- <i>sama</i> died instantly.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:23.040
Let's hold a press conference
before the media finds out.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.290
The information from the scene is still chaotic

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.370
and the police are still putting
things together at the station.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.290
Hey, it's on the way.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.120
Can we stop at home real quick?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.790
We won't be able to go home for a while, I bet.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.200
Get back!

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.870
Out of the way!

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:50.370
Inspector! Inspector Lestrade!

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:51.700
John!

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.250
Mary- <i>san</i> !

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.580
--What's wro--
--John!

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.120
I need your help!

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:04.500
You're safe.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.410
No luck. The communicator isn't working.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.870
We're getting in touch with everybody.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.700
We know Kobayashi's on his way, but--

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:16.250
You don't know where Lucy is.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.410
How'd you know?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.790
I'll be right back.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.410
Welcome home.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.120
I'm glad you're safe.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.410
Thanks.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:39.660
I think Dad and I will be
at the police station for a while.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.790
Can you get him a change of clothes?

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:43.870
Understood.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.200
James- <i>sama</i> !

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.620
We're so glad you're safe!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.370
Thanks.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.660
James- <i>sama</i> ?

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.200
What are you doing?

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.830
Oh, well...

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.080
Dad said he wanted me to get some documents.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:45.910
But he said to let no one into this room.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.910
Why did he go after me?

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.540
He's clearly interested in attention.

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:58.040
It's unlikely he has any personal hatred of you.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:02.660
Who is it?

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:04.620
Carlyle.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.620
She wants to talk about James.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.830
Get the press conference ready.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.290
I'll send someone to get you immediately.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:19.790
So she put transmitters on all the detectives?

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:25.040
Yes. The stupid-looking badges on your shirts.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:28.540
Was she trying to steal the glory for herself?

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.620
Does that mean she's going after Albert?

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.830
Maybe. Maybe not.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:39.250
Why put transmitters on us?

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:45.870
When this job came, Moriarty wanted
everybody in the row house on it.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:48.830
Did he?

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.660
But what of it?

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:54.040
Actually, is James okay?

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.620
Put it on speaker.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.910
Okay.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.700
Hello?

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.080
James! You're safe!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.410
I'm so glad.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:09.370
"James"

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:09.370
Huh? Sherlock hasn't told you yet?

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:11.950
Of course I'm safe.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.330
This whole thing was my doing.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.250
What is he talking about?

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.750
Lucy's with Albert, right?

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.160
Smart!

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:25.950
You're the only one I can
have fun with, Sherlock!

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.250
Let's talk again soon.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:29.950
Follow this.

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.080
Quickly!

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:33.370
What? What? Follow what?

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:35.750
Fifty million!

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:36.660
--You're in a hurry, huh, Sherlock?

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.950
--If this is a waste of time, you owe me big.
--You're in a hurry, huh, Sherlock?

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:40.370
--I'm borrowing this.
--Oh, did you think you could fool Mrs. Hudson?

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.500
--I'll go, too.
--Oh, did you think you could fool Mrs. Hudson?

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.700
--I want to talk to him alone.
--Hello?

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:45.620
But...

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.790
Please, Hudson.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:59.700
Hey, Moriarty.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.250
What's wrong?

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:03.700
Answer me!

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:08.250
Carl--

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.120
James!

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.660
Moriarty, you're there, right?

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:43.580
James, you...

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:46.830
Don't worry. It's just a muscle relaxant.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.200
Hey, what are you doing?

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:51.410
--Sorry, Sherlock. I'm busy.

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:54.160
--What are you after?
--Sorry, Sherlock. I'm busy.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.000
You know the answer to that.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.700
Hang on a second.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.910
This whole study's in such bad taste.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.160
Tell me the code to the safe.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:09.950
That's right.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:11.910
You're scared.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.580
Of me.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:16.620
You figured it out before anyone.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:20.500
That the real me was empty.

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:25.790
Let's say the heart is a tea pot.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:29.620
Everybody fills that pot
with conscience and morals,

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:31.370
and takes good care of it.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:34.830
But my tea pot has a hole in it.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:39.200
No matter how much conscience
my parents and teachers pour into it...

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.870
...it all just leaks out the bottom.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.040
James, you always--

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.370
Honey...

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:57.000
I'm sorry.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.870
It's okay.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:06.330
I don't want you getting hurt,
so don't touch it.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:08.370
Here, James!

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:16.660
Alex and Mom treated me like a normal boy.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:19.040
And I tried to convince myself that I was.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:20.250
But...

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.750
Don't worry. It'll stop soon.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.000
Okay...

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:34.870
I'll go take a look!

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.330
James!

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.950
Dry yourself off, okay?

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.540
Okay!

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:24.160
What's wrong?

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:28.250
Mom, I'll make you wonderful!

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:41.410
I killed Mom.

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:45.040
But it wasn't because I wanted to kill her.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.450
I don't know...

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:49.450
I was just curious what would happen.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:54.290
I was sure it would be beautiful.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:08.910
It's okay.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:10.910
Don't cry.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:15.160
It's not that Dad hates you.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:18.120
He's just sad Mom's gone.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:19.450
So...

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.450
But he says I'm not normal.

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:24.790
That I'm creepy!

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:28.660
We're twins, right?

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:33.620
So I know more about you than anybody.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:36.000
You're not creepy!

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.660
You're just a normal boy!

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.790
Now stand up!

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:46.700
Or I'll get mad, James!

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:57.000
In this world, I'm here,
you're here, Dad's here...

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:58.450
People we're close to are here!

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:00.450
People we don't know are here!

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:04.450
We're all different. We're all unique.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.200
So don't worry!

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:11.660
Living... Living with a lot
of different people...

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.500
...is a wonderful thing, isn't it?

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:17.870
I'll always love you, James.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.830
So I hope you'll love this world, too!

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:25.620
Or I'll...

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:27.620
Or I'll get mad!

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:35.540
Alex was always beside me.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.500
Cheering me up.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:41.660
So I thought I had to try my best to be normal.

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:45.250
But no matter how much
Alex tried to patch the hole,

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:47.750
or fill it with good things,

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:54.540
the water just kept pouring out
and emptying my teapot.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:57.580
And when Alex was killed,

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.830
a strange feeling came over me.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:05.330
Her death made me so sad, so frustrated...

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:08.500
But it wasn't just that.

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:14.660
And then I realized...

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:19.580
That I hated Jack because
he took my prey, Alex from me!

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:24.410
That it was Alex I wanted
to destroy more than anything!

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:31.620
I felt so free...

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:36.290
For the first time in my life,
I felt like I could be proud of who I was!

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:44.700
I tried killing a few people in the prison.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:46.580
And I made other people kill, too.

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:49.080
And it was so much fun!

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:51.870
I couldn't stop!

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:01.700
James, don't hurt me!

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:03.410
I'm sorry! Please don't hurt me!

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:05.080
Why are you apologizing?

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:08.750
I'm just who you thought I was!

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:10.410
You're amazing!

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:13.410
You understood me better than Mom.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.580
Better than Alex!

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:31.540
Now, tell me the code to the safe.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:35.250
Please, don't kill me!

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:43.790
Hurry up. What's the code?

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:46.750
I wanted to start over with you.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:50.750
You got me out of jail to help you
with your election, right?

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:53.660
No, I wanted to...

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.580
Just give it to me.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.290
Lie and I kill you on the spot.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:09.120
Right, 13... three times...

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:12.410
Right, 79... once.

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:15.660
Left, 53... twice.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:20.950
Damn it. I was never interested
in you from the start.

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:33.580
You used Jack to kill this many people, huh?

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:36.040
My name's here.

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:38.750
No, Jack threatened me...

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:39.950
Idiot.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:42.700
Your excuses are so cheap.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:52.000
So you did have it.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.580
That's...

00:17:57.290 --> 00:18:02.910
Alex tried to seal the hole in
my teapot and fill it with good things.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:07.370
But that only appeared
to be a solution on the surface.

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:13.660
So with our broken teapots,
could we ever be fulfilled?

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:18.120
No, it's simple. If a pot's got a crack...

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:23.790
...just shatter it!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.330
"Mrs. Hudson"

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.500
"Mrs. Hudson"

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.500
I figured out, actually, that if it's got a hole in it,

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:33.080
"Mrs. Hudson"

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:33.080
you're better off not having it at all!

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:36.500
So I have to destroy Sherlock, too.

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.700
It's very simple.

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:48.370
Just kill someone one time.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:51.330
And if one time isn't enough...

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:55.160
Kill two people.

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:01.540
Alexandra...

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.410
We're finally out.

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:12.660
After the stadium incident,

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:15.500
they're sure careful about who they let through.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.950
Hurry. I'll pay twice the normal fee!

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:26.200
What do you mean?

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:30.330
Just kill Watson in three hours.
And send me a picture.

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:31.950
Thanks!

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.950
Is Lucy- <i>san</i> here?

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:45.080
I'm sorry, John.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:58.500
It's Moriarty, right?

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:02.660
The stadium bomb was his doing, too.

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:08.040
Fine. Kill me.

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:23.040
Lucy- <i>san</i> !

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:30.870
That's blood.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.160
Are you okay?

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:33.950
There's no time for that!

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.750
Call an ambulance!

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.160
Sorry about that.

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:16.250
The battery ran out.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.200
Where are you?

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:19.370
Where do you think?

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:23.410
I'm not there anymore.

00:21:23.410 --> 00:21:25.410
What did you mean by that?

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:29.870
That what Alex was to you, Watson was to me.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:36.160
That Watson's trying to fill
your tea pot with good things.

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:38.950
Just like what Alex did with me.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:43.750
Oh, there may have been a better way.

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:47.080
The best way, the one I couldn't do...

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.000
Where are you?

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.870
Tell me!

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:08.120
Sherlock!

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.160
I'm sorry!

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:49.910
"Not Breathing"

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:51.830
"Today's Kitty BAR Pipe Cat's Popular Cat, Pipe"
"He's actually the second cat owned by Mrs. Hudson;
the first was his mom, who is now deceased."
